WEBVTT

STYLE
::cue(c.color9CD5FF) { color: #9CD5FF; }

1
00:00:01.000 --> 00:00:07.000 line:5% align:center
<b><c.color9CD5FF>One Pace Addon</c></b>

2
00:01:33.070 --> 00:01:38.030
[NARRATOR]
Lush, green forests
as far as the eye can see.

3
00:01:38.030 --> 00:01:41.200
A gentle stream with
crystal-clear water.

4
00:01:41.200 --> 00:01:44.750
Flowers and plants
teeming with color and life.

5
00:01:44.750 --> 00:01:47.380
Beautiful beaches
in every region.

6
00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.210
This is a tale of
the Land of Wano,

7
00:01:50.210 --> 00:01:53.420
when its skies were clear
and its people flourished

8
00:01:53.420 --> 00:01:57.010
in a paradise secluded
from the world.

9
00:01:56.670 --> 00:01:59.590
<b>Teahouse</b>

10
00:01:57.010 --> 00:01:59.850
[OTSURU]
You're saying that
a mountain was chasing you?

11
00:01:59.850 --> 00:02:00.970
[TOWNSPERSON G]
That's right!

12
00:02:00.970 --> 00:02:03.520
And the thing was
groaning at us, too!

13
00:02:03.520 --> 00:02:05.230
An ill omen!

14
00:02:05.230 --> 00:02:09.150
Perhaps you awakened
the wrath of the Mountain God!

15
00:02:09.150 --> 00:02:11.530
[giggles]
Just kidding!

16
00:02:11.530 --> 00:02:15.070
But you look quite happy after
such a frightful encounter!

17
00:02:15.030 --> 00:02:19.660
<b>Miss Tsuru,

Waitress



Teahouse

in the

Mountains</b>

18
00:02:15.070 --> 00:02:16.610
What else happened?

19
00:02:16.610 --> 00:02:19.630
[TOWNSPERSON H]
Can't fool you,
huh? We finally caught it!

20
00:02:19.630 --> 00:02:20.630
[gasps]

21
00:02:20.240 --> 00:02:21.370
[shrieks]

22
00:02:21.370 --> 00:02:22.750
Huh?

23
00:02:27.720 --> 00:02:31.060
[gasps]
What an
adorable little boar!

24
00:02:31.060 --> 00:02:32.400
[TOWNSPERSON I]
If we take it to the capital,

25
00:02:32.400 --> 00:02:34.190
we'll get a platinum
coin for him!

26
00:02:34.190 --> 00:02:34.640
[OTSURU]
What?

27
00:02:34.640 --> 00:02:37.730
You could buy a house
with that kind of money!

28
00:02:38.900 --> 00:02:40.860
[TOWNSPERSON G]
The boss of
the Kurokuma Family has been

29
00:02:40.860 --> 00:02:42.820
looking for a white boar to put
on display in his storefront.

30
00:02:42.820 --> 00:02:46.530
He had a reward poster
put out for it and everything.

31
00:02:47.700 --> 00:02:49.070
[OTSURU]
But he shouldn't
put it on display!

32
00:02:49.070 --> 00:02:53.240
White boars are divine
messengers, not decorations!

33
00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:55.870
[gasps]

34
00:02:55.870 --> 00:02:57.120
[OTSURU]
Hm?

35
00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:58.630
[gasps]

36
00:02:58.630 --> 00:03:00.130
[OTSURU]
Kin'emon!

37
00:03:00.130 --> 00:03:02.000
[KIN'EMON]
Ow, ow, ow!

38
00:03:01.700 --> 00:03:08.080
<b>Kin'emon

Local Thug</b>

39
00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:04.720
Stealing money from
our shop again, are you?

40
00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:07.550
Tsuru! We've known
each other since childhood,

41
00:03:07.550 --> 00:03:09.010
give me a break here!

42
00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:11.600
We're like family, you can
spare a little money for me!

43
00:03:11.600 --> 00:03:13.560
You're just going to
gamble it all away!

44
00:03:13.560 --> 00:03:16.980
Do you know how much owe me?
Because I certainly do!

45
00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.810
[screams]

46
00:03:20.230 --> 00:03:24.530
The next time you lay your
filthy fingers on my money,

47
00:03:24.530 --> 00:03:29.160
I'll sell your organs
to cover the debt!

48
00:03:29.160 --> 00:03:30.780
If you can't pay me back,

49
00:03:30.780 --> 00:03:34.290
I'll take your clothes
as collateral!

50
00:03:33.820 --> 00:03:39.530
<b>The Day of the Mountain God</b>

51
00:03:39.530 --> 00:03:42.450
<b>Katsuzo</b>

52
00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:45.830
<b>Crematorium

Flower 
Capital</b>

53
00:03:43.870 --> 00:03:45.910
[TOWNSPERSON J]
Oh, please don't cry, my dear!

54
00:03:45.910 --> 00:03:47.370
Although, a funeral is

55
00:03:47.370 --> 00:03:49.580
the proper place
for that, I suppose.

56
00:03:49.580 --> 00:03:50.960
Did something happen?

57
00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:52.880
Not with the service, no.

58
00:03:52.880 --> 00:03:54.670
But after the cremation,
when we were about to

59
00:03:54.670 --> 00:03:57.920
gather up my father's bones,
he showed up!

60
00:03:57.920 --> 00:03:59.670
[TOWNSPERSON K]
He put a pot
on top of the remains

61
00:03:59.670 --> 00:04:02.670
and started cooking
oden with the fire!

62
00:04:08.300 --> 00:04:09.970
[BANZABURO]
It seems the young Lord Oden

63
00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.100
has no talent for sailing.

64
00:04:12.100 --> 00:04:13.930
As of today, he has attempted to

65
00:04:13.930 --> 00:04:17.730
leave the country
illegally 38 times.

66
00:04:17.730 --> 00:04:20.440
Rather impressive
that he survived.

67
00:04:20.440 --> 00:04:22.070
[BANZABURO]
I suspect that
you know much of this,

68
00:04:22.070 --> 00:04:23.530
but allow me to offer a glimpse

69
00:04:23.530 --> 00:04:26.280
into some of your son's
"accomplishments."

70
00:04:25.830 --> 00:04:28.790
<b>Kozuki Sukiyaki

Shogun of Wano
(Oden's Father)</b>

71
00:04:26.530 --> 00:04:26.840
Before he was even a year old,
he sent his nanny flying.

72
00:04:26.840 --> 00:04:30.430
Before he was even a year old,
he sent his nanny flying!

73
00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:32.240
When he was two,
he was swift enough

74
00:04:32.240 --> 00:04:34.540
to catch two hares at once.

75
00:04:34.540 --> 00:04:34.840
When he was four,

76
00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:35.830
When he was four,
he knocked out a bear!

77
00:04:35.830 --> 00:04:38.540
he hurled a boulder
and knocked out a bear!

78
00:04:38.540 --> 00:04:40.670
When he was six,
he spent all his time

79
00:04:40.670 --> 00:04:43.130
at the pleasure halls,
wasting royal money.

80
00:04:43.130 --> 00:04:44.760
When he was eight,
for some reason,

81
00:04:45.890 --> 00:04:47.600
he instigated a fight
with a bunch of

82
00:04:47.600 --> 00:04:48.880
violent patrons at
a gambling parlor.

83
00:04:48.880 --> 00:04:50.800
He defeated them all, naturally.

84
00:04:50.800 --> 00:04:52.180
By the time he was nine,

85
00:04:52.180 --> 00:04:54.980
he was blacklisted
by the yakuza.

86
00:04:54.980 --> 00:04:57.350
He repaid this slight by
burning down the gambling hall

87
00:04:57.350 --> 00:05:00.100
he was banned from,
instigating a gang war.

88
00:05:00.100 --> 00:05:02.690
Then, at the ripe age
of ten years old,

89
00:05:02.690 --> 00:05:04.980
he was arrested for assault.

90
00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.860
Sent to the quarries
as punishment,

91
00:05:06.860 --> 00:05:08.400
he developed an
impressive talent

92
00:05:08.400 --> 00:05:10.570
while serving his sentence.

93
00:05:10.570 --> 00:05:14.080
That is to say, he became
a master stonemason in no time!

94
00:05:14.080 --> 00:05:17.620
Thanks, of course,
to his Kozuki blood!

95
00:05:18.660 --> 00:05:22.330
[BANZABURO]
From there, he left
prison and reformed his ways!

96
00:05:22.330 --> 00:05:24.590
Then, there's the tale
of the drought!

97
00:05:24.590 --> 00:05:26.420
When wells were drying
up in the capital,

98
00:05:26.420 --> 00:05:30.430
he couldn't bear the sight
of people suffering.

99
00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:31.800
[BANZABURO]
So, when he was 14,

100
00:05:31.800 --> 00:05:34.720
he redirected the river
to run through the city.

101
00:05:36.390 --> 00:05:38.680
[BANZABURO]
This caused a massive flood,

102
00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:41.060
and an arrest warrant
was issued again.

103
00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:42.480
[Sukiyaki sighs]

104
00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:46.150
This was his cue to flee,
so he traversed that river,

105
00:05:46.150 --> 00:05:49.610
in hopes of escaping
the country by sea!

106
00:05:50.740 --> 00:05:53.740
[BANZABURO]
Needless to say,
he failed miserably!

107
00:05:54.080 --> 00:05:56.540
Then, when he was 15,
he threatened a priest

108
00:05:56.540 --> 00:05:59.120
to let him hide in
a mountain temple.

109
00:05:59.120 --> 00:06:02.250
He brought back women
from the capital every night.

110
00:06:02.250 --> 00:06:05.170
Before long he had
his own harem!

111
00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:10.220
This is clearly the work
of a monster and not a man.

112
00:06:10.220 --> 00:06:13.380
That said, although he did
acquire a great many lovers,

113
00:06:13.380 --> 00:06:15.930
they were free to
leave at any time.

114
00:06:15.930 --> 00:06:19.600
Of course, not everyone
involved was quite so happy!

115
00:06:19.600 --> 00:06:21.730
The women's boyfriends
for example,

116
00:06:21.730 --> 00:06:24.150
and their parents,
and their husbands!

117
00:06:24.150 --> 00:06:27.900
A team of skillful samurai
even joined their cause!

118
00:06:29.820 --> 00:06:31.820
[BANZABURO]
The young lord
welcomed their challenge

119
00:06:31.820 --> 00:06:33.820
and stood his ground!

120
00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.240
[BANZABURO]
This later came to
be known as the Harem War!

121
00:06:38.240 --> 00:06:41.080
The Hyogoro Family
attempted to restore peace,

122
00:06:41.080 --> 00:06:42.410
but when all attempts failed,

123
00:06:42.410 --> 00:06:45.540
they were drawn into
the chaos of battle as well!

124
00:06:45.540 --> 00:06:46.750
[SUKIYAKI]
I've heard enough!

125
00:06:46.750 --> 00:06:48.090
[gasps]

126
00:06:48.090 --> 00:06:52.130
Right. The young lord
is now 18 years old.

127
00:06:52.130 --> 00:06:55.760
He continues to stir up trouble
at a healthy pace to this day.

128
00:06:55.760 --> 00:06:57.300
Report over.

129
00:06:56.930 --> 00:07:00.810
<b>Notice 
of
 Disownment</b>

130
00:06:57.300 --> 00:06:59.180
[SUKIYAKI]
I need you to
deliver this to Oden

131
00:06:59.180 --> 00:07:01.230
without speaking on the matter.

132
00:07:00.810 --> 00:07:01.480
<b>Notice 
of
 Disownment</b>

133
00:07:01.230 --> 00:07:02.560
[Kin'emon grunts]

134
00:07:02.250 --> 00:07:04.660
[Townsperson I groans]

135
00:07:04.660 --> 00:07:07.120
[KIN'EMON]
It's like
I just won the lottery!

136
00:07:07.120 --> 00:07:10.000
My lucky star's
shining on me today!

137
00:07:10.500 --> 00:07:15.220
If I give this to old boss
Kurokoma, I'll be rich!

138
00:07:17.240 --> 00:07:18.590
[Kin'emon sneezes]
Hey, while we're at it,

139
00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:20.800
how 'bout you give me
all your clothes?

140
00:07:23.850 --> 00:07:25.850
[Kin'emon grunts]

141
00:07:25.850 --> 00:07:27.690
[YAKUZA MEMBER A]
You're not
getting away this time!

142
00:07:27.690 --> 00:07:30.400
[KIN'EMON]
Whoa, whoa, whoa!
Wait! Gimme a break!

143
00:07:30.400 --> 00:07:31.860
I'll pay you guys back today!

144
00:07:31.860 --> 00:07:33.240
I'm about to hit it big!

145
00:07:33.240 --> 00:07:34.860
[YAKUZA MEMBER B]
More excuses!

146
00:07:34.860 --> 00:07:38.610
[KIN'EMON]
It's true! Just let
me go to the Kurokoma mansion!

147
00:07:39.160 --> 00:07:41.870
[HYOGORO]
Kin'emon? Oh, him?

148
00:07:41.870 --> 00:07:44.700
That little thug
who stole our money?

149
00:07:44.700 --> 00:07:46.710
Well, here's an easy solution.

150
00:07:45.490 --> 00:07:51.330
<b>Hyogoro 
"the Flower"


Man of Chivalry, 
Flower Capital</b>

151
00:07:46.710 --> 00:07:49.040
Catch him and fillet him alive!

152
00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:51.500
But don't engage him one-on-one.

153
00:07:51.500 --> 00:07:55.920
He's a punk, but he's
strong. Real strong.

154
00:07:57.630 --> 00:08:00.140
I have been entrusted
with 60 silver!

155
00:08:00.140 --> 00:08:03.640
But simply spending it
would be a waste, right?

156
00:08:05.350 --> 00:08:07.480
[DENJIRO]
I'll take this pot here.

157
00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:10.970
<b>30
Silver</b>
<b>60
Silver</b>

158
00:08:07.770 --> 00:08:09.350
I'm running an errand
for someone.

159
00:08:09.350 --> 00:08:11.980
All right. That'll be 30 silver.

160
00:08:10.970 --> 00:08:11.510
<b>30
Silver</b>
<b>60
Silver</b>

161
00:08:11.980 --> 00:08:14.860
– [DENJIRO] Here.
– [VENDOR A] Thanks, kid.

162
00:08:14.860 --> 00:08:17.530
[DENJIRO]
Oops! I bought the wrong pot.

163
00:08:17.530 --> 00:08:19.280
I need the bigger one.

164
00:08:19.280 --> 00:08:23.030
[Vendor A sighs]
All right,
but that one is 60 silver.

165
